# Phase 0 & 1: Software Engineering, Python & Data Foundations

This folder covers the entire foundational stage of my journey toward becoming an AI Engineer. Starting from basic C++ knowledge, the goal here is to master the essential developer tools, Python programming, data manipulation, testing, and backend APIs required before diving into Machine Learning.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack & Learning Resources

* **Developer Environment & Git ([The Missing Semester of Your CS Education](https://missing-semester-esp.github.io/)):** Used to master the command-line shell, terminal workflows, debugging, and version control with Git.
* **Core Python ([30 Days of Python](https://github.com/asabeneh/30-days-of-python)):** Used to build fluency in Python syntax, data structures, object-oriented programming (OOP), file handling, and virtual environments.
* **Relational Databases ([SQLBolt](https://sqlbolt.com/)):** Used to query, filter, join, and structure data stored in SQL databases.
* **Data Analysis & Visualization ([freeCodeCamp - Data Analysis with Python](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/data-analysis-with-python/)):** Used to clean, transform, and visualize datasets using **NumPy**, **Pandas**, and **Matplotlib**.
* **Automated Testing ([pytest](https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html)):** Used to write unit and functional tests, verifying code reliability with assertions, exception handling, and fixtures.
* **Backend & APIs ([FastAPI](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/)):** Used to build validated REST APIs capable of connecting to databases and serving data or AI models.

## ⚙️ How This Folder Is Structured (Nodes)

Each topic is broken down into modular **nodes** containing study notes, hands-on exercises, and mini-projects:

1. **`01_dev_environment_git`** — Command-line navigation, shell scripting, debugging, and Git workflows.
2. **`02_python_fundamentals`** — Python core concepts, data structures, OOP, and virtual environment management.
3. **`03_sql_databases`** — Writing SQL queries, multi-table `JOIN`s, aggregations, and table design.
4. **`04_data_analysis`** — Numerical computing with NumPy, data manipulation with Pandas, and plotting with Matplotlib (via freeCodeCamp).
5. **`05_testing_pytest`** — Writing automated test suites to validate scripts and data pipelines.
6. **`06_apis_fastapi`** — Designing endpoints, request/response validation, and database integration.

